tein kinase A signalling. The three most frequently cisplatinated penta-nucleotide motifs and genomic region are CTGGG, CCAGG and GCTGG, and promoter, respectively. Among the CDGs are 1330 enzyme, 747 transcription regulator and 486 transporter genes. Importantly, cisplatin targeted 306 protein kinase genes, accounting for 59% of putative protein kinase genes in the human genome, and 92 protein phosphatase genes. This indicates that cisplatin genome-wide disturbs protein phosphorylation. This data set contains the original sequencing data of two biological replicates, matching results to the hg38 genome, and the analysis results of the distribution of the damage areas identified by the two sequencing results.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-06-23T16:25:54.448Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dmyfkn7pnz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/dmyfkn7pnz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Fuyi","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Gene"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":117901,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":129,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":117901,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":117408,"restricted":62,"embargoed":431},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2013},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":608},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":451},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":383},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":378},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":376},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S.